Hey guys,

Wrote a small program several years ago to make my Nethacking a little
easier, and I put it online if anyone is interested (completely free
of course).

I have ascended a couple of times, but I still die a lot, and I got
tired of selecting all my info and options every time I restarted. So,
I wrote this program for Nethack for Windows (you have to be playing
with the NethackW.exe file). What it does is allow you to define
character templates (as many as you like), where you predefine your
name, class/role, race, alignment, and a few pickup options (for
example, if I'm playing a Wizard or Rogue, I like to autopickup all
the daggers I throw).

From then on, instead of starting Nethack, I just start this program,
select the character I want to play with a single click, and press
start. The program sets up your options file, runs Hearse for you, and
starts (or resumes) the game for you.

It probably only saves you 8 or 9 clicks in total, but as much as I
die, I like being able to single click restart the same character, or
switch to a different one without reslecting everything and resetting
my pickup options every single game.

If you're interested, just unzip the file in your nethack install
directory. You'll need to set up Hearse at least 1 time if you never
have before, just like you normally would, but once you do that, the
process is automated.

Wrote it for myself, but if anyone else finds it useful, then I
consider it a bonus :)

